        "original_id": "55222708-3c6d-5db8-b9b8-a0ddad28524e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Deanna Loveland, Simon Cowell, Fantasia Barrino\n- Companies: Target Corporation, Toyota, USA Weekend Magazine, Walmart\n- Places: United States, Skyline Mall\n- Roles: recording artist, harpist, pianist, fashion designer\n- Works: \"Shine\", \"A Pure Country Gift II\", \"Country Strong\"\n- Topics: songwriting competitions, talent agencies, discount retail\n\nFacts:\n- Deanna Marie Loveland was born on April 5, 1989, and she is an American recording artist, harpist, pianist, and fashion designer.\n- In 2002, Target Corporation purchased Skyline Mall and replaced most of the complex with a Target store, leaving only a second-level fitness center.\n- In 2005, Deanna Loveland's original song \"Shine\" was named 1st Runner-Up among 12,000 entries in USA Weekend Magazine's national songwriting competition judged by Simon Cowell and Fantasia Barrino.\n- A month after that competition result, Deanna Loveland signed with a talent agency and appeared in music videos, commercials for Toyota and Target, and the films \"A Pure Country Gift II\" and \"Country Strong.\"\n- Target Corporation is the second-largest discount store retailer in the United States after Walmart, and it is a component of the S&P 500 Index.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "83ef9728-8a98-5b38-9f83-5cbe120c8723",
        "text": "Page: Deanna Loveland. Sentence: Deanna Marie Loveland (born April 5, 1989) is an American recording artist, harpist, pianist and fashion designer.\nPage: Deanna Loveland. Sentence: Consequently, she began songwriting and in 2005 her original song, \"Shine\" was 1st Runner-Up out of 12,000 entries in USA Weekend Magazine's national songwriting competition judged by Simon Cowell and Fantasia Barrino.\nPage: Deanna Loveland. Sentence: A month later she signed with a talent agency, appearing in music videos and commercials for companies including Toyota and Target and films including \"A Pure Country Gift II\" and \"Country Strong\".\nPage: Target Corporation. Sentence: Target Corporation is the second-largest discount store retailer in the United States, behind Walmart, and a component of the S&P 500 Index.\nPage: Skyline Mall. Sentence: The mall was purchased in 2002 by discount retailer Target Corporation, who replaced the majority of the complex (except for a fitness center on the second level) with a Target store.",
